      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "body": "Reopening. Closing this was premature, and the reason is worth recording so it does not happen again.\n\nI closed this on the basis that #4344 had resolved the storm and that exponential backoff was a remaining refinement tracked by #4340. #4340 was then closed as superseded by #4344. Each closure assumed the other one covered the backoff, so it never landed.\n\nState on current `main` (`e71a5f99c`):\n\n- What survived: jitter, coalesced retries, the generation guard, and the degraded state after repeated failures. That part of my closing comment still holds.\n- What did not: there is still no growth and no ceiling. `workspace-file-events.ts` waits 5s +/- 1s, and `event-transport.ts` and `notifications.ts` wait a flat 5s. Jitter only spreads retries inside a two second window; it does not lower the rate, so every stream still knocks every ~5s for as long as the daemon keeps refusing it. That is the amplification this issue describes.\n- Also gone: #4344's `sse-parse.ts` and its fetch-based reader are no longer in the tree. #4388 rewrote `workspace-file-events.ts` back to native `EventSource`.\n\nTwo pieces are outstanding, which is why this stays open rather than being closed by either one:\n\n- Renderer backoff: #4826, open, CI green. Bounded exponential backoff shared across all three SSE consumers.\n- Daemon side: #4334, still open. Maps transient DB-busy and deadline errors to 503 instead of an opaque 500, which is the `Retry-After`-adjacent half of the suggested fix above.\n\nClosing this once both have landed.",
