    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Summary\nThe renderer opens Server-Sent-Events streams \u2014 `GET /api/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/events` and `/api/v1/notifications/stream` \u2014 with `EventSource`, which reconnects **immediately on any failed connection, with no backoff**. If the daemon returns a transient 5xx while *setting up* the stream, the client reconnects in a tight loop, turning one brief failure into a sustained burst of failed requests and high CPU on both sides.\n\n## Where it happens\n- Handler: `backend/internal/httpd/controllers/sessions.go` \u2192 `streamWorkspaceChanges` (and the notifications stream controller). These can only return 5xx during setup, before `w.WriteHeader(200)`.\n- Setup failure points: `WorkspaceWatchPaths` \u2192 `sessionWorkspaceRecord` (its `GetSession` branch wraps the error untyped as `fmt.Errorf(\"get %s: %w\", \u2026)` \u2192 500), and `workspacewatch.Watch` / `watchRoot`.\n- Renderer: the `EventSource` consumer for these streams reconnects with no backoff.\n\n## Reproduction\nThe daemon port is in `~/.ao/running.json`.\n1. Healthy stream (baseline): `curl -N http://127.0.0.1:<port>/api/v1/sessions/<id>/workspace/events` \u2192 `200`, stream stays open. \u2705 verified\n2. Missing workspace: same call for a session whose workspace dir is gone \u2192 `404 SESSION_WORKSPACE_NOT_FOUND` (already typed on current `main`). \u2705 verified \u2014 so the common missing-path case is *not* the culprit.\n3. Trigger the amplification: put the daemon under DB-lock contention (see #3963) so `GetSession` intermittently errors \u2192 stream setup returns `500` \u2192 watch the renderer immediately reconnect and re-fail in a loop (visible in the access log and as CPU spikes). A single stuck stream produces a large, self-sustaining burst.\n\n## Suggested fix\n- Renderer: exponential backoff + jitter on SSE reconnect; stop reconnecting when the session is terminated and on any `4xx`.\n- Daemon (optional): send `Retry-After` on transient setup failures so clients pace reconnects.\n\n## Related\n- #3963 (DB lock contention \u2192 the transient 5xx this amplifies)\n- #1321 (RFC: remove polling \u2192 reactive sync)\n",
